108:     Connect same-colored foreground components with one-cell-wide orthogonal paths around teal wall segments.
109: 
110:     Input structure
111:     - The dominant color is the background.
112:     - Teal cells are fixed wall segments and are never source connectors.
113:     - Other foreground colors appear as one or more 4-connected components; colors with a single component stay unchanged.
114: 
115:     Rule
116:     - For each non-background, non-teal color, read its 4-connected components in row-major order.
117:     - Connect each consecutive pair by the shortest clear L-shaped path between the two components.
118:     - Clear paths may pass only through background or the same color, and they preserve the previous travel axis when both bends are possible.
119: 
120:     Key insight
121:     - The output is not a global recolor: each color traces a routed chain through its own components while teal cells and other colors act as blockers.
122:     """
